\begin{definition}[Random oracle combiner, informal; Dodis, Ferguson, Goldin, Hall, and Pietrzak]\label{def:roc2}
A combiner $C^{h_1,h_2}_{\mathcal Z}\colon\{0,1\}^m\to\{0,1\}^n$ is a secure random oracle combiner if, for every oracle circuit $g$, both $C^{\mathcal H,g^{\mathcal H}}_{\mathcal Z}$ and $C^{g^{\mathcal H},\mathcal H}_{\mathcal Z}$ are indifferentiable from a fresh random oracle $\mathcal G\colon\{0,1\}^m\to\{0,1\}^n$, over the random choice of the salt $\mathcal Z$, against every polynomial-query distinguisher.
\end{definition}

