Let $\widetilde C^{h_1,h_2}_{\mathcal Z_1,\mathcal Z_2}(M) := h_1^*(M,\mathcal Z_1)\oplus h_2^*(M,\mathcal Z_2)$ be as above, and let $\lambda$ be the security parameter. This paper proves $\widetilde C$ is a secure random oracle combiner (Definition~\ref{def:roc2}) whenever $|\mathcal Z_1|,|\mathcal Z_2| > |M|+\lambda$. Resolve which of the following holds:
\begin{itemize}
\item[(i)] There is a choice of $|\mathcal Z_1|,|\mathcal Z_2| = O(1)$ blocks, independent of $|M|$, together with an efficient adversary breaking the indifferentiability of $\widetilde C$ from a random oracle; or
\item[(ii)] $\widetilde C$ remains a secure random oracle combiner even when $|\mathcal Z_1|,|\mathcal Z_2|$ are a constant number of blocks, independent of $|M|$.
\end{itemize}
